"donor_log2fc":0.0656874,"donor_lfcse":0.100119,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00624694}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000206527","module":"pink","kme":0.216903,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":1.0,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000206527","module":"blue","kme":0.119588,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.906476,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000206527","entrez_id":["201562"],"uniprot":["Q6Y1H2"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene can catalyze the third step (dehydration) in the conversion of long chain fatty acids to very long chain fatty acids. The encoded protein localizes to the endoplasmic reticulum membrane. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2016].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6Y1H2","text":"Catalyzes the third of the very long-chain fatty acids (VLCFA) elongation four-step cycle (condensation, reduction, dehydration, and reduction). This endoplasmic reticulum-elongation process is characterized by the addition of two carbons to the lipid chain through each cycle. This enzyme catalyzes the dehydration of the 3-hydroxyacyl-CoA intermediate into trans-2,3-enoyl-CoA, within each cycle of elongation. Therefore, it participates in the production of various VLCFAs involved in multiple biological processes as precursors of membrane lipids and lipid mediators."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}